["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A grouse lives by its eyes and ears. Learn what it sees and hears and you get the close, calm shot instead of a roar of wings behind a tree.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 330\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of a grouse head and its field of view, using chicken data as a close cousin, 75 percent. Each eye covers a wide side wedge, for about 300 degrees in total. Only a narrow 30 degree wedge straight ahead is seen with both eyes. A small blind spot sits straight behind.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"330\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">What a grouse sees (top view)</text>\n<path d=\"M200 182 L231.1 66.1 A120 120 0 0 1 231.1 297.9 Z\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" opacity=\"1\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 182 L168.9 297.9 A120 120 0 0 1 168.9 66.1 Z\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" opacity=\"1\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 182 L231.1 297.9 A120 120 0 0 1 168.9 297.9 Z\" fill=\"#e5e5e5\" opacity=\"1\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 182 L168.9 66.1 A120 120 0 0 1 231.1 66.1 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0.8\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"188\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"168\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><polygon points=\"196,160 200,150 204,160\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n<circle cx=\"192\" cy=\"167\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#23261f\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"208\" cy=\"167\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#23261f\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Both eyes: about 30 degrees</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Left eye</text>\n<text x=\"380\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Right eye</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Blind spot behind</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Total view:</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">about 300</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"298\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">degrees</text>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Chicken data,</text>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">a close cousin</text>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"298\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">(75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Eyes on the sides: a huge field of view, little overlap <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Sees colour and motion very well <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the eyes</summary><ul><li>Grouse are galliform birds, close cousins of the chicken. Most eye studies are on chickens; treat these as a guide for grouse <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Field of view about 300 degrees, with only about 30 degrees seen by both eyes (75%, chicken data; Martin's review of bird visual fields gives 20 to 30 degrees for most birds).</li><li>A small blind spot sits straight behind the head <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Colour: four kinds of single cones (violet, blue, green, red), one more than us. Birds see colours we cannot (75%, PLOS One study on chickens).</li><li>Motion: a double cone is thought to handle motion <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. A grouse notices movement before shape (Tip, 70%).</li><li>Night: grouse roost at night in trees, on the ground or in snow <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. How well they see in the dark: no source found (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 330\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A spruce tree with a dark spruce grouse sitting on a branch close to the trunk, circled in orange. It looks like a dark blob near the trunk with the tail hanging down. Tip: look up slowly; midday is the time.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"330\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spot a grouse sitting in a tree</text>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"38\" width=\"384\" height=\"232\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e9eef0\"/>\n<path d=\"M8 250 C80 240 160 246 240 244 C300 242 350 246 392 240 V270 H8z\" fill=\"#cfd8b8\"/>\n<rect x=\"135\" y=\"60\" width=\"10\" height=\"196\" fill=\"#5c4030\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 52 Q151.0 59.7 162.0 76.0 L162.0 72.3 L157.1 80.6 L152.2 75.8 L147.3 81.5 L142.4 73.4 L137.6 76.4 L132.7 71.9 L127.8 78.4 L122.9 71.6 L118.0 77.4 Q129.0 59.7 140 52z\" fill=\"#2e4a2c\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 56 Q149.0 61.4 158.0 73.4 L158.0 69.6 L154.0 78.2 L150.0 73.2 L146.0 78.4 L142.0 74.0 L138.0 74.7 L134.0 69.0 L130.0 74.4 L126.0 70.1 L122.0 76.6 Q131.0 61.4 140 56z\" fill=\"#3d5f37\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 66 Q158.0 74.4 176.0 92.0 L176.0 88.1 L168.0 95.0 L160.0 91.0 L152.0 95.6 L144.0 87.5 L136.0 97.3 L128.0 92.1 L120.0 96.4 L112.0 90.8 L104.0 93.9 Q122.0 74.4 140 66z\" fill=\"#2e4a2c\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 70 Q154.8 75.9 169.5 88.8 L169.5 88.9 L163.0 94.1 L156.4 87.2 L149.8 94.3 L143.3 85.6 L136.7 92.1 L130.2 89.0 L123.6 94.4 L117.0 84.3 L110.5 91.6 Q125.2 75.9 140 70z\" fill=\"#3d5f37\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 84 Q165.0 93.1 190.0 112.0 L190.0 110.8 L178.9 112.3 L167.8 107.3 L156.7 116.9 L145.6 108.8 L134.4 113.0 L123.3 109.6 L112.2 115.6 L101.1 109.5 L90.0 115.1 Q115.0 93.1 140 84z\" fill=\"#2e4a2c\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 88 Q160.5 94.4 181.0 108.2 L181.0 104.9 L171.9 112.0 L162.8 104.4 L153.7 110.7 L144.6 104.4 L135.4 114.2 L126.3 105.3 L117.2 111.0 L108.1 106.4 L99.0 109.9 Q119.5 94.4 140 88z\" fill=\"#3d5f37\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 104 Q171.0 113.8 202.0 134.0 L202.0 132.7 L188.2 138.6 L174.4 130.4 L160.7 134.4 L146.9 129.6 L133.1 139.4 L119.3 132.4 L105.6 135.9 L91.8 133.5 L78.0 136.1 Q109.0 113.8 140 104z\" fill=\"#2e4a2c\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 108 Q165.4 114.9 190.8 129.6 L190.8 130.4 L179.5 134.0 L168.2 130.3 L156.9 135.0 L145.6 128.8 L134.4 129.9 L123.1 127.4 L111.8 130.7 L100.5 126.6 L89.2 131.0 Q114.6 114.9 140 108z\" fill=\"#3d5f37\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 126 Q177.0 136.5 214.0 158.0 L214.0 154.1 L197.6 159.8 L181.1 157.9 L164.7 161.7 L148.2 158.7 L131.8 160.5 L115.3 157.7 L98.9 163.8 L82.4 154.7 L66.0 158.1 Q103.0 136.5 140 126z\" fill=\"#2e4a2c\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 130 Q170.3 137.3 200.7 153.0 L200.7 150.2 L187.2 157.7 L173.7 149.0 L160.2 153.3 L146.7 148.1 L133.3 155.0 L119.8 153.8 L106.3 155.3 L92.8 148.8 L79.3 155.7 Q109.7 137.3 140 130z\" fill=\"#3d5f37\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 150 Q184.0 161.2 228.0 184.0 L228.0 179.9 L208.4 188.1 L188.9 180.0 L169.3 184.3 L149.8 179.4 L130.2 185.2 L110.7 181.5 L91.1 189.9 L71.6 179.6 L52.0 185.7 Q96.0 161.2 140 150z\" fill=\"#2e4a2c\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 154 Q176.1 161.8 212.2 178.4 L212.2 176.3 L196.1 184.3 L180.1 175.9 L164.1 183.0 L148.0 176.6 L132.0 179.1 L115.9 179.4 L99.9 179.9 L83.9 176.3 L67.8 178.6 Q103.9 161.8 140 154z\" fill=\"#3d5f37\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 176 Q190.0 187.9 240.0 212.0 L240.0 208.5 L217.8 212.2 L195.6 210.0 L173.3 217.0 L151.1 212.3 L128.9 213.5 L106.7 209.5 L84.4 212.2 L62.2 209.5 L40.0 213.5 Q90.0 187.9 140 176z\" fill=\"#2e4a2c\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 180 Q181.0 188.3 222.0 205.8 L222.0 203.2 L203.8 211.7 L185.6 204.2 L167.3 211.4 L149.1 201.1 L130.9 206.7 L112.7 206.0 L94.4 207.2 L76.2 202.0 L58.0 207.3 Q99.0 188.3 140 180z\" fill=\"#3d5f37\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 204 Q196.0 215.9 252.0 240.0 L252.0 240.5 L227.1 245.4 L202.2 240.2 L177.3 241.3 L152.4 235.6 L127.6 243.0 L102.7 239.5 L77.8 244.7 L52.9 238.9 L28.0 245.4 Q84.0 215.9 140 204z\" fill=\"#2e4a2c\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 208 Q185.9 216.3 231.8 233.8 L231.8 234.3 L211.4 235.4 L191.0 232.9 L170.6 237.7 L150.2 232.0 L129.8 238.7 L109.4 232.7 L89.0 238.6 L68.6 232.7 L48.2 235.8 Q94.1 216.3 140 208z\" fill=\"#3d5f37\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 40 L134 58 L146 58z\" fill=\"#2e4a2c\"/>\n<path d=\"M174.1 156.0 L177.9 166.4 L171.4 173.5 L173.9 187.8 L162.9 186.3 L160.2 198.0 L152.2 194.9 L146.0 203.0 L139.7 195.2 L130.9 200.7 L130.3 184.1 L120.2 185.4 L121.6 172.8 L112.5 166.9 L118.6 156.0 L111.3 144.7 L122.9 140.1 L120.6 127.1 L128.5 124.7 L131.9 114.1 L139.8 117.2 L146.0 109.0 L152.2 117.5 L161.2 110.8 L163.4 124.9 L172.8 125.4 L171.1 138.7 L178.3 145.5z\" fill=\"#22381f\"/>\n<rect x=\"136\" y=\"110\" width=\"8\" height=\"88\" fill=\"#5c4030\"/>\n<path d=\"M144 159 L184 164\" stroke=\"#4a3426\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(158 150)\"><path d=\"M-4 4 C-8 14 -9 26 -6 36 L2 36 C3 26 4 14 4 6z\" fill=\"#2a2a27\"/><path d=\"M-6 33 L2 33 L2 36 L-6 36z\" fill=\"#a0582a\"/><ellipse cx=\"2\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"11\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#3b3b37\"/><path d=\"M-3 -8 C0 -4 2 4 0 10\" stroke=\"#6b6b62\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" fill=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"6\" cy=\"-15\" r=\"6.4\" fill=\"#2a2a27\"/><path d=\"M3 -19 C5 -21 8 -21 10 -19\" stroke=\"#d1342a\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M12 -16 L16 -14.6 L12 -13.6z\" fill=\"#1b1d1a\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-15.5\" r=\"1.2\" fill=\"#e8e2d0\"/><path d=\"M-2 10 L-4 12 M4 10 L6 12\" stroke=\"#4a3426\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/></g>\n<circle cx=\"159\" cy=\"156\" r=\"32\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3.4\"/>\n<line x1=\"191\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"238\" y2=\"136\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><circle cx=\"191\" cy=\"150\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"237.5\" y=\"118.0\" width=\"124.9\" height=\"49.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"300\" y=\"138.5\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A dark blob</text>\n<text x=\"300\" y=\"158.5\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">near the trunk</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tail hangs down. Look up, slowly.</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"318\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#b8450a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Midday is the time (Tip).</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Move slow, stop behind trees, never skyline yourself (Tip).</li><li>Look for a shape and a twitch, not a whole bird (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how hunters use this</summary><ul><li>Your blaze orange does not hurt you much: grouse key on movement more than colour (Tip, 60%). Wear what the law and safety need.</li><li>Walk, stop, look. The stop is when you see the bird and the bird sees no motion (Tip).</li><li>In trees: scan near the trunk on the sunny side of conifers. A grouse is a dark blob with a tail hanging down (Tip).</li><li>On the ground: look for a head moving through the leaves, then freeze (Tip).</li><li>Old hand's rule (tradition): \"See the eye, not the bird.\"</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 310\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Sound chart on a frequency scale from 10 hertz to 10 kilohertz. Most birds hear best between 1 and 4 kilohertz. The grouse inner ear is tuned to low sounds below 1 kilohertz. The ruffed grouse drum is under 100 hertz. Tip: low thumps carry, like boots on rock, truck doors and voices, so talk softly and shut doors gently.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"310\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">What grouse hear</text>\n<line x1=\"30\" y1=\"226\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"226\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<line x1=\"30.0\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"30.0\" y2=\"232\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"30.0\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10 Hz</text>\n<line x1=\"143.33333333333331\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"143.33333333333331\" y2=\"232\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"143.33333333333331\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100 Hz</text>\n<line x1=\"256.66666666666663\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"256.66666666666663\" y2=\"232\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"256.66666666666663\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1 kHz</text>\n<line x1=\"370.0\" y1=\"220\" x2=\"370.0\" y2=\"232\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"370.0\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10 kHz</text>\n<text x=\"84.07374220156174\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ruffed drum: under 100 Hz</text>\n<rect x=\"84.07374220156174\" y=\"78\" width=\"54.07374220156174\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fbe3d3\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"143.33333333333331\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Grouse inner ear: tuned below 1 kHz</text>\n<rect x=\"143.33333333333331\" y=\"132\" width=\"113.33333333333331\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8ecd9\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"324.9001323505024\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Most birds hear best: 1 to 4 kHz</text>\n<rect x=\"256.66666666666663\" y=\"184\" width=\"68.23346568383579\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Low thumps carry: boots on rock, truck doors,</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"298\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">voices. Talk soft, shut doors gently (Tip).</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Most birds hear best at 1 to 4 kHz <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Grouse ears are tuned to low sounds <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what grouse hear</summary><ul><li>Bird hearing is sharpest between 1 and 4 kHz, about where we hear best (70%, bird hearing reviews).</li><li>Gallinaceous birds (grouse, quail, chickens) have an inner ear tuned lower, below 1 kHz <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Chickens hear very low sounds, under 64 Hz, better than people <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>The ruffed grouse drum is a very low sound, under 100 Hz <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>. Other grouse hear it a long way off.</li><li>What carries to a grouse: boots on rock, a slammed truck door, a dropped tailgate, voices (Tip).</li><li>Tip: close doors gently, talk in a whisper, and do not crunch along a gravel road edge.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, top view. Wind blows from the grouse toward you. The grouse scent drifts downwind in a widening cone. Your dog zig zags into the wind, crosses the scent cone, turns up it and closes on the grouse. Point or flush: be ready.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Your dog works into the wind</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"260\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n<g><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"270.0\" y2=\"70.0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"270.0,70.0 279.0,65.7 279.0,74.3\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;-20 0;0 0\" dur=\"2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g>\n<g><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"270.0\" y2=\"120.0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"270.0,120.0 279.0,115.7 279.0,124.3\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;-20 0;0 0\" dur=\"2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Wind</text>\n<path d=\"M300 170 L80 110 L80 230 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".18\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(300 170)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"8\" rx=\"30\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(302 168) scale(0.55 0.55)\"><polygon points=\"-20,-6 -38,-20 -48,-12 -52,0 -48,8 -20,8\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M-40 -18 Q-50 -10 -48 6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><circle cx=\"21\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"16,-20 20,-28 25,-20\" fill=\"#9a6b45\"/><polygon points=\"28,-16 35,-13 28,-10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"23\" cy=\"-16\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 11 M10 13 l2 11\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n<text x=\"300\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Grouse</text>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Scent drifts downwind</text>\n<path id=\"mgr-dog-wind-p\" d=\"M40 280 L120 250 L40 210 L130 175 L170 168 L240 170\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 6\"/>\n<g><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><animateMotion dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\" rotate=\"auto\"><mpath href=\"#mgr-dog-wind-p\"/></animateMotion></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hits the scent!</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"48\" width=\"230\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"125\" y=\"69\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Point or flush: be ready</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Your dog finds the scent cone downwind. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>No study found that grouse smell people (Tip).</li><li>Wind matters for sound and for your dog's nose (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: wind and thermals for a grouse hunter</summary><ul><li>Birds of the grouse family are not known for a strong sense of smell. We found no source showing grouse detect hunters by scent (Tip, so treat smell as a minor factor).</li><li>Wind carries your noise toward or away from the bird (Tip).</li><li>Wind and rising or sinking air (thermals) carry the bird's scent to your dog. Work a dog into the wind so it meets the scent cone (Tip, common dog handling advice).</li><li>Thermals: air rises up slopes when the sun warms them and sinks at evening (80%, see <a href=\"#/s/wind-thermals\">Wind and thermals</a>).</li><li>Strong wind seems to make grouse wild. Hunters blame noise that hides predators (hunter lore, 60%). See <a href=\"#/s/mc-grouse-06\">The day</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 330\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The grouse escape plan in 5 steps. 1: freeze and trust the camouflage. 2: walk or run off under cover. 3: flush with a roar of wings. 4: glide, usually under 90 metres or 100 yards. 5: land in a tree or cover and freeze again.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"330\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Grouse escape plan: 5 steps</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"46\" width=\"372\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<circle cx=\"36\" cy=\"69\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"36\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text>\n<text x=\"58\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Freeze. Trust the camouflage.</text>\n<rect x=\"28\" y=\"102\" width=\"358\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"125\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"50\" y=\"131\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text>\n<text x=\"72\" y=\"131\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Walk or run off under cover.</text>\n<rect x=\"42\" y=\"158\" width=\"344\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fbe3d3\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"181\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"64\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text>\n<text x=\"86\" y=\"187\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Flush with a roar of wings.</text>\n<rect x=\"56\" y=\"214\" width=\"330\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<circle cx=\"78\" cy=\"237\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"78\" y=\"243\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text>\n<text x=\"100\" y=\"243\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Glide, usually under 90 m (100 yd).</text>\n<rect x=\"70\" y=\"270\" width=\"316\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<circle cx=\"92\" cy=\"293\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"92\" y=\"299\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">5</text>\n<text x=\"114\" y=\"299\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Land in a tree or cover. Freeze again.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>First defence: camouflage and stillness <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Last: a roaring flush and a short glide to cover <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the escape plan, in detail</summary><ul><li>Spruce grouse rely on camouflage and stillness and often let people close <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Ruffed grouse often walk or run away under cover before they fly (Tip, 65%).</li><li>The flush is loud on purpose: the roar startles a predator (Tip, 60%).</li><li>After the flush a ruffed grouse glides, usually under 90 m (100 yd), and often lands in a tree (75%, Pennsylvania Game Commission; Outdoor Life).</li><li>Then it freezes again. That is why a follow up works (Tip). See <a href=\"#/s/mc-grouse-04\">The mind</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, side view of a forest edge. You walk slowly along the edge. You stop and stand still. The grouse hiding ahead cannot stand the silence and flushes with a roar of wings, climbing up and away over the trees. Up and away with sky behind it is the safe shot. Tip: the stop makes the bird flush.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"200\" width=\"400\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"170\" width=\"400\" height=\"34\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" opacity=\".5\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\" transform=\"translate(40 200) scale(1.4)\"><polygon points=\"-12,0 0,-34 12,0\"/><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"0\" width=\"6\" height=\"8\"/></g>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\" transform=\"translate(360 200) scale(1.6)\"><polygon points=\"-12,0 0,-34 12,0\"/><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"0\" width=\"6\" height=\"8\"/></g>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\" transform=\"translate(300 196) scale(1.1)\"><polygon points=\"-12,0 0,-34 12,0\"/><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"0\" width=\"6\" height=\"8\"/></g>\n  <g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(1.0)\"><circle r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><rect x=\"-6\" y=\"8\" width=\"12\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"40 216;160 216;160 216\" keyTimes=\"0;.45;1\" dur=\"8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n  <g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.8)\"><path d=\"M-18 -4 L-30 -14.0 L-30 2 Z\" fill=\"#8a7560\"/><ellipse rx=\"22\" ry=\"15\" fill=\"#8a7560\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-14\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#8a7560\"/><path d=\"M14 -24 Q20 -36 26 -30\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M26 -15 L32 -13 L26 -11Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-4 14 L-6 24 M6 14 L8 24\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"250 196;250 196;290 130;340 96\" keyTimes=\"0;.62;.8;1\" dur=\"8s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"6.4s\"/><path d=\"M230 170 l-14 -10 M240 160 l-6 -16 M262 160 l6 -16 M272 170 l14 -10\"/></g>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"380\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <g><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"3.6s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Walk slowly along the edge</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"3.6s\"/><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"5s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stop. Stand still...</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5s\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The stop makes it flush (Tip)</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"7.2s\"/><rect x=\"190\" y=\"240\" width=\"204\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"292\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Up and away, sky behind:</text><text x=\"292\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">now it is a safe shot</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Walk, stop, wait. The stop flushes the bird. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Walk slow, stop often: the silence makes the bird nervous (Tip).</li><li>Be ready when you stop, not when you walk (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why the stop works (hunter lore)</summary><ul><li>Many hunting writers say a grouse holds while you keep walking past, then flushes when you stop, because a stopped predator may have seen it (hunter lore, 60%).</li><li>Stop next to an opening with room to swing, not in the thick of it (Tip).</li><li>Hold the gun at ready during the stop (Tip).</li><li>Circle a lone evergreen: a grouse under it may walk to the far side and flush from there (Tip, Outdoor Canada).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 330\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of a grouse head and its field of view, using chicken data as a close cousin, 75 percent. Each eye covers a wide side wedge, for about 300 degrees in total. Only a narrow 30 degree wedge straight ahead is seen with both eyes. A small blind spot sits straight behind.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"330\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">What a grouse sees (top view)</text>\n<path d=\"M200 182 L231.1 66.1 A120 120 0 0 1 231.1 297.9 Z\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" opacity=\"1\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 182 L168.9 297.9 A120 120 0 0 1 168.9 66.1 Z\" fill=\"#cfe0ef\" opacity=\"1\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 182 L231.1 297.9 A120 120 0 0 1 168.9 297.9 Z\" fill=\"#e5e5e5\" opacity=\"1\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 182 L168.9 66.1 A120 120 0 0 1 231.1 66.1 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0.8\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"200\" cy=\"188\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"168\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><polygon points=\"196,160 200,150 204,160\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n<circle cx=\"192\" cy=\"167\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#23261f\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<circle cx=\"208\" cy=\"167\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#23261f\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Both eyes: about 30 degrees</text>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Left eye</text>\n<text x=\"380\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Right eye</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Blind spot behind</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Total view:</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">about 300</text>\n<text x=\"10\" y=\"298\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">degrees</text>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">Chicken data,</text>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">a close cousin</text>\n<text x=\"390\" y=\"298\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\">(75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Rhyme: \"It sees you move, it hears you step, it never smells the sweat you've kept.\"</li><li>Number trick: \"300 to see, 30 to judge\": 300 degree view, 30 degrees with both eyes.</li><li>Old hand's rule (tradition): \"Walk like you're late, stop like you're lost.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li>\"Stop where you can swing.\"</li><li>\"Doors soft, voices low.\"</li><li>\"Dog into the wind, you behind the dog.\"</li><li>These are memory lines made for this course and widely repeated hunter habits, not science.</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>Chicken vision and bird hearing studies, Pennsylvania Game Commission, hunting writers. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source</summary><ul><li>Kram, Mantey and Corbo, avian cone photoreceptors (PLOS One), search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://research.birmingham.ac.uk/en/publications/visual-fields-and-their-functions-in-birds\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Martin, Visual fields and their functions in birds</a>, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Bird hearing: reviews of avian audiograms, chicken and quail studies, ruffed grouse inner ear abstract, search previews (65 to 70%).</li><li><a href=\"https://www.pa.gov/agencies/pgc/wildlife/discover-pa-wildlife/ruffed-grouse\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Pennsylvania Game Commission, Ruffed grouse</a>, read directly <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.outdoorlife.com/articles/hunting/2007/09/hit-or-miss-grouse\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outdoor Life, Hit or miss grouse</a>, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.outdoorcanada.ca/?p=68\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Outdoor Canada, Ruffed grouse tips</a>, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://idfg.idaho.gov/press/field-forest-grouse\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Idaho Fish and Game, Field and forest grouse</a>, read directly <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>All checked 2026-10-11. <a href=\"#/sources\">Hunt Mentor research notes (summary of the sources listed in Sources)</a>.</li></ul></details>"]